As you might know, I have recently been working with Accessibility API intensively!

From **_Getting Text Cursor (Caret) Position_** to **_Text Contents Near Text Cursor (Caret)_** !

What do I want in this article? Some generic information on the active application! The tabs, the content!

The idea is pretty simple! We loop just like we would with HTML DOM! However, as we all know by now, the document for AccessibilityAPI is basically the same as not-existing!

## Basic Steps

1. Create a system-wide accessibility object with `[AXUIElementCreateSystemWide](https://developer.apple.
com/documentation/applicationservices/1462095-axuielementcreatesystemwide)` . In general, this `AXUIElement` will have two attributes available, `kAXFocusedUIElementAttribute` and `kAXFocusedApplicationAttribute` . I will be sharing with you two different approaches, traversing down from the `kAXFocusedApplicationAttribute` and up from `kAXFocusedUIElementAttribute` .
2. Call `[AXUIElementCopyAttributeValue](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applicationservices/1462085-axuielementcopyattributevalue)` on either `kAXFocusedUIElementAttribute` or `kAXFocusedApplicationAttribute` to get an `AXUIElement` .
3. Get the attributes available on the element using `AXUIElementCopyAttributeNames` (or `AXUIElementCopyParameterizedAttributeNames` for parameterized ones such as range, bounds, and etc. I am not interested in those in this article here but the idea is the same).
4. Get attributes value with `[AXUIElementCopyAttributeValue](https://developer.apple.

